                <TR><TD>HttpTokens=required blocks unauthenticated GET to IMDS endpoint.</TD></TR>
                <TR><TD>Containers must issue a signed PUT to obtain a token first.</TD></TR>
                <TR><TD>HopLimit=1 prevents token TTL traversal beyond the EC2 host.</TD></TR>
                <TR><TD><B>Control 2 — SSRF Mitigation in API Gateway Tier:</B></TD></TR>
                <TR><TD>AWS WAF rule blocks requests targeting 169.254.169.254.</TD></TR>
                <TR><TD>Input validation on URL parameters enforces an allowlist;</TD></TR>
                <TR><TD>internal IP ranges including link-local are denied.</TD></TR>
                <TR><TD><B>Control 3 — NACL Egress Block (Defense-in-Depth):</B></TD></TR>
                <TR><TD>NACLs deny outbound traffic to 169.254.169.254/32 port 80</TD></TR>
                <TR><TD>at the subnet level for all container workload subnets.</TD></TR>
                <TR><TD><B>Control 4 — Least-Privilege Instance Profiles:</B></TD></TR>
                <TR><TD>Instance roles scoped to minimum permissions; no iam:PassRole,</TD></TR>
                <TR><TD>no s3:GetObject on PCI-DSS data buckets, no sts:AssumeRole wildcard.</TD></TR>
